From: "Barak A. Pearlmutter" <barak+git@pearlmutter.net>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 11:32:22 +0100
Subject: disparPDFc: a link to disparPDF, instead of a second build of it

disparPDF and disparPDFc were built from the same sources, differing
only in COMPARA_IS_CONSOLE, which put disparPDFc always in batch mode.
In ConfrontaPDF's qmake build it was also a Windows console program
and not a macOS bundle, but the CMake build kept only the second; and
the only thing it is needed for is a plain executable that scripts on
macOS can run, since the disparPDF command Homebrew installs launches
the bundle with "open", which passes back neither the output nor the
exit status.

So build the program once, and have it decide from the name it was run
by (argv[0], ignoring case and .exe; applicationFilePath() would
resolve the link) whether to be disparPDFc.  disparPDFc is installed as
a symbolic link to disparPDF, or on macOS to the program in the bundle,
or on Windows as a copy; the build directory has one too, for the tests
and the manual page, which are unchanged.  The Homebrew formula links
bin/disparPDFc to the program in the bundle, which runs it directly,
and its test runs disparPDFc --version (not tried on macOS).

New tests: disparPDFc compares in batch mode without -b, also when run
by a link named DisparPDFC.exe.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01DFo7ywK1YasqiQ8A3v7kVX
